{"agency_id": "climate-change-commission", "canonical_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xHm7CxR2s3g", "captured_at": "2026-06-25T07:47:48+00:00", "content": "Webinar: Monitoring report: Emissions reduction (2025)\n\nIs NZ on track to meet its emissions reductions goals? In this webinar, Chief Executive Jo Hendy and Project Director Rob Carr dive into the Climate Change Commission's latest report. This yearly report tracks the progress the country is making towards meeting its emissions budgets and the 2050 emissions reduction target.\n\nThe full report, summaries and technical documents are available on our website: https://www.climatecommission.govt.nz/erm-2025?utm_source=youtube.com&amp;utm_campaign=erm-2025&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_content=webinar\n\nYou can find today's presentation slides on our Webinars page: https://www.climatecommission.govt.nz/get-involved/watch/webinars?utm_source=youtube.com&amp;utm_campaign=erm-2025&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_content=webinar\n\nSign up to get alerts about our upcoming webinars: https://confirmsubscription.com/h/t/2DB84EBFF23E1BC9\n\nCHAPTERS:\n\n00:00 Overview - Jo Hendy, Chief Executive\n00:25 The Commission's role: what we do and why\n04:04 Our approach to this year's report\n05:27 How our work all fits together\n\n07:44 Our findings - Rob Carr, Project Director\n09:30 Risks\n11:26 Opportunities\n13:09 Recommendation\n14:07 What's next?\n\nQ&amp;A\n15:00 Can New Zealand still achieve the 2050 target?\n16:06 Can New Zealand afford climate action, given high cost of living?\n18:06 How the Commission's benchmarks have changed since last year's report\n19:33 Do the emissions budgets meet the NDCs?\n21:09 What modes of freight should be prioritised?\n23:25 Shifting farming practices\n25:16 What are the best ways to incentivise electrifying everything?\n27:08 What policies have been considered to address electricity generation?\n28:21 Is the electricity market fit for purpose (e.g. dry year risk, ease of entry for generators)?\n31:50 Transport emissions are down due to the rise of working from home and the recession, but these could reverse. Was this taken into account?\n32:57 How much potential is there to reduce emissions in the transport sector? Which technologies and urban design options have the greatest potential?\n35:10 Military emissions\n36:06 Improvements in emissions accounting methodology\n37:46 Carbon capture and storage (CCS)\n40:30 Forestry and forests\n43:40 What's one overseas emissions reduction policy New Zealand should adopt?\n45:10 Nature based solutions\n46:58 Policies for improving energy efficiency\n48:31 Mitigation options that could not be modelled but have potential\n49:38 Any recommendations for educators at secondary school and tertiary levels?\n50:39 Methane reduction opportunities", "content_hash": "ec01b197cdc69700a5acecf7b208ca3d31a35f5c1f0f93f07497598f69e01b11", "cross_source_ids": {"channel_id": "UCvAJ21jjC9ynnMJ5rq0ZxVQ", "feed_url": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCvAJ21jjC9ynnMJ5rq0ZxVQ", "source_id": "climate-change-commission-youtube-ac260476", "video_id": "xHm7CxR2s3g"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_youtube_channel_rss", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2025-07-30T03:39:02+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\youtube\\2025-07\\f71dd09a29ba44bba61439b2.json", "record_id": "youtube:f71dd09a29ba44bba61439b2", "source_account": "UCvAJ21jjC9ynnMJ5rq0ZxVQ", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "youtube", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCvAJ21jjC9ynnMJ5rq0ZxVQ"}
